WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.825
Welcome to Navigation General.

2
00:00:03.075 --> 00:00:07.275
This module answers three questions a captain asks all day.

3
00:00:07.525 --> 00:00:09.125
Where am I?

4
00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:11.350
What’s the water doing?

5
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.950
And what’s the weather about to do?

6
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:23.125
It covers more ground than any other part of the exam, so we’ll take it one piece at a time, and we start with the most basic piece: position.

7
00:00:23.375 --> 00:00:25.200
Look at the diagram.

8
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:31.875
Latitude measures how far north or south of the equator you are, from zero to ninety degrees.

9
00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:39.775
Longitude measures how far east or west you are of the prime meridian at Greenwich, from zero to one hundred eighty.

10
00:00:40.025 --> 00:00:43.025
Each degree divides into sixty minutes.

11
00:00:43.275 --> 00:00:49.100
On the chart, latitude is read on the side scales, and longitude on the top and bottom.

12
00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.350
So which do you write first?

13
00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:54.000
Latitude.

14
00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:55.750
Always.

15
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.075
And here’s an easy check.

16
00:00:58.325 --> 00:01:02.400
All of Florida is north latitude and west longitude.

17
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.750
If your answer says east, something went wrong.
